@startuml architecture-mushroom-mood-target
title Mushroom Mood Target Architecture Flow

' Status: Planned
' Purpose: Show the planned main boundaries for the broader Mushroom Mood flow, including saved spots, observation-backed seasonality, and restricted species management.

actor User
actor "Restricted Admin" as Admin
participant "Start, Weather, and Mushroom Pages" as AppUi
participant "Mushroom Readiness API Route" as ReadinessRoute
participant "Readiness Service" as ReadinessService
database "Saved Spot Store" as SavedSpotStore
database "Supported Species Catalog" as SpeciesCatalog
database "Species Profile Rules" as SpeciesProfileRules
participant "Weather History Repository" as WeatherHistoryRepository
participant "Seasonal Observation Repository" as SeasonalObservationRepository
database "Seasonal Evidence Cache" as SeasonalEvidenceCache
participant "SMHI API" as SmhiApi
participant "ArtDatabanken Observation Search API" as ObservationSearchApi
participant "ArtDatabanken Taxon Search API" as TaxonSearchApi
participant "Species Management API Route" as SpeciesManagementRoute

User -> AppUi: Choose spot and species
AppUi -> ReadinessRoute: Request readiness, confidence, and explanation data
ReadinessRoute -> ReadinessService: Build result for selected spot and species
ReadinessService -> SavedSpotStore: Load saved spot context when relevant
ReadinessService -> SpeciesCatalog: Load supported species metadata
ReadinessService -> SpeciesProfileRules: Load species-specific timing and sensitivity rules
ReadinessService -> WeatherHistoryRepository: Load recent weather evidence for the spot
WeatherHistoryRepository -> SmhiApi: Fetch or refresh weather data
SmhiApi --> WeatherHistoryRepository: Weather history data
ReadinessService -> SeasonalObservationRepository: Load seasonal observation evidence near the spot
SeasonalObservationRepository -> SpeciesCatalog: Read stored taxon ID for supported species
SeasonalObservationRepository -> SeasonalEvidenceCache: Read derived evidence by taxon, spot, radius, and time policy

alt Fresh derived evidence is cached
  SeasonalEvidenceCache --> SeasonalObservationRepository: Fresh processed seasonal evidence
else Cache is missing or expired
  SeasonalObservationRepository -> ObservationSearchApi: Search observations by taxon ID, spot, radius, and time policy
  ObservationSearchApi --> SeasonalObservationRepository: Seasonal observation data
  SeasonalObservationRepository -> SeasonalEvidenceCache: Store processed seasonal evidence with TTL
  SeasonalEvidenceCache --> SeasonalObservationRepository: Cached processed seasonal evidence
else Live refresh fails but stale cache is reusable
  SeasonalEvidenceCache --> SeasonalObservationRepository: Stale processed seasonal evidence with freshness limitation
end

alt Required inputs are available
  ReadinessService -> ReadinessService: Combine seasonal, weather, and species-profile factors
  ReadinessService --> ReadinessRoute: Readiness label, probability, confidence, and explanation inputs
  ReadinessRoute --> AppUi: 200 OK result payload
  AppUi --> User: Show main result and deeper explanation views
else Inputs are partial or missing
  ReadinessService -> SpeciesProfileRules: Fall back to static seasonal timing when observation evidence is weak or unavailable
  ReadinessService --> ReadinessRoute: Low-confidence or unavailable result with missing-data reasons
  ReadinessRoute --> AppUi: Result payload with limitations
  AppUi --> User: Show low-confidence or unavailable state
end

Admin -> AppUi: Open restricted species management
AppUi -> SpeciesManagementRoute: Search taxon and save supported species
SpeciesManagementRoute -> TaxonSearchApi: Search and confirm external taxon identity
TaxonSearchApi --> SpeciesManagementRoute: Matching taxa
SpeciesManagementRoute -> SpeciesCatalog: Create or update supported species entry with stored taxon ID
SpeciesManagementRoute -> SpeciesProfileRules: Create or update species-specific rules
SpeciesManagementRoute --> AppUi: Confirm catalog update

note right of SpeciesProfileRules
Detailed expert submission and approval workflow
is intentionally deferred.
This diagram only fixes the stable boundary where
species-specific rules are stored and adjusted.
end note

note right of SpeciesCatalog
Supported species store the external taxon ID
needed for runtime observation lookup.
Runtime readiness must not call taxon search.
end note

note right of SeasonalEvidenceCache
Cache stores processed seasonal evidence,
not raw observation payloads.
Long-run target: persistent cache.
Initial shortcut: in-memory cache if needed.
end note

note right of ReadinessService
If seasonal evidence is sparse, missing, or unavailable
without reusable stale cache, the service falls back
to the static species calendar and lowers confidence.
end note

@enduml